  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Full Lap – long curve, pass and one-timer",
  "description": "A line in each corner: A and B by the top goal, C and D by the bottom one. A goalkeeper in both goals. A runs in a long curve down along the boards and in towards the middle of the other half and gets a pass from line D. A carries the ball forward, passes up to B in the corner and sprints towards goal. In the slot A gets a pass back and shoots first time.\n\nAt the same time D does the same the other way: long curve, pass from line A, pass to C and a one-timer at the bottom goal. Then B and C start.\n\nRotation: A to B, B to A, C to D and D to C. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Play the passes into the runner's path so they keep their speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Sprint towards goal straight after the pass to the corner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time in the slot – the shots should hit the target."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
